    'latest resolves to the last executed block, not the last accepted one (blocks/access.go:133-134). safe and finalized resolve to the last settled block (blocks/access.go:135-136). pending resolves to the last accepted block only when api-resolve-pending-to-last-executed is false; the C-Chain default is true (cchain/config.go:138, blocks/access.go:125-127), and a node with it false refuses state for pending (sae/rpc/stateful.go:79-83). An explicit number is accepted up to the last accepted block and refused above it (blocks/access.go:139-146). Every state method then opens the post-execution root of the resolved block through restoreExecutedBlock, which waits for execution of an accepted block (sae/rpc/blocks.go:59-86, WaitUntilExecuted at line 82), and the header handed to the EVM is rewritten to carry that post-execution root and the executed base fee (sae/rpc/stateful.go:537-542). debug_traceCall uses the same post-execution state (traceCallBackend, sae/rpc/stateful.go:578-580). So no tag names a block whose state does not exist: latest is executed by construction, and a number between latest and the accepted tip blocks until it is executed. The cycle 24 statement that latest is the last accepted block is corrected by this reading; the eth_call results of earlier cycles at latest ran on executed post-state with the same interpreter configuration (vm.Config{}) as block execution (saexec/execution.go:360).',
